          "type": "object"
        }
      ]
    },
    "FxFyCxCy": {
      "description": "Standard pinhole intrinsics: focal lengths and principal point in pixels.\n\nThe pixel grid is assumed orthogonal, so `K` carries no skew term.",
      "properties": {
        "cx": {
          "description": "Principal point X coordinate in pixels.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "cy": {
          "description": "Principal point Y coordinate in pixels.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "fx": {
          "description": "Focal length in pixels along X.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "fy": {
          "description": "Focal length in pixels along Y.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "fx",
        "fy",
        "cx",
        "cy"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Iso3Schema": {
      "description": "JSON Schema proxy for [`Iso3`] (`nalgebra::Isometry3<f64>`).\n\n`nalgebra` does not implement [`schemars::JsonSchema`], so `*Export` and\nparameter types that embed [`Iso3`] annotate the field with\n`#[cfg_attr(feature = \"schemars\", schemars(with = \"Iso3Schema\"))]`\n(or `Vec<Iso3Schema>` / `Option<Iso3Schema>`). This proxy mirrors the exact\nserde wire format of `Isometry3`:\n`{ \"rotation\": [qx, qy, qz, qw], \"translation\": [tx, ty, tz] }`.\n\nIt exists only to describe that shape to `schemars`; it is never\nconstructed at runtime.",
      "properties": {
        "rotation": {
          "description": "Unit quaternion `[qx, qy, qz, qw]` (i, j, k, w order).",
          "items": {
            "format": "double",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "maxItems": 4,
          "minItems": 4,
          "type": "array"
        },
        "translation": {
          "description": "Translation `[tx, ty, tz]` in meters.",
          "items": {
            "format": "double",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "maxItems": 3,
          "minItems": 3,
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "rotation",
        "translation"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "LaserPlane": {
      "description": "Laser plane in camera frame: unit normal + signed distance.\n\nThe plane equation is: n̂ · p + d = 0\nwhere p is a point in camera coordinates.",
      "properties": {
        "distance": {
          "description": "Signed distance from camera origin",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "normal": {
          "description": "Unit normal vector in camera frame. Serializes as `[nx, ny, nz]`.",
          "items": {
            "format": "double",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "maxItems": 3,
          "minItems": 3,
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "normal",
        "distance"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PointCovariance": {
      "description": "The covariance of one observed image point, px²: the symmetric matrix\n`[[xx, xy], [xy, yy]]`.\n\nIt states the point's measurement noise. A calibration whose views carry\ncovariances weighs each reprojection residual by its inverse (it\n*whitens* it): an uncertain point counts less, and an elongated one is\ntrusted more across its long axis than along it. A uniform weight `w` on\nevery point corresponds to the covariance `I / w`.\n\nConstructed only through [`PointCovariance::new`] (or deserialization),\nwhich checks that it is finite and positive definite.\n\n# Example\n\n```\nuse vision_calibration_core::PointCovariance;\n\n// σ = 0.3 px along u, 0.1 px along v, uncorrelated.\nlet cov = PointCovariance::new(0.09, 0.0, 0.01).unwrap();\nassert_eq!(cov.yy(), 0.01);\nassert!(PointCovariance::new(1.0, 2.0, 1.0).is_err()); // not positive definite\n```",
      "properties": {
        "xx": {
          "description": "Variance along the image `u` axis, px².",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "xy": {
          "description": "Covariance of `u` and `v`, px².",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "yy": {
          "description": "Variance along the image `v` axis, px².",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "xx",
        "xy",
        "yy"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ProjectionParams": {
      "description": "Serializable projection model parameters.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "description": "Classic pinhole model.",
          "properties": {
            "type": {
              "const": "pinhole",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "type"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "description": "Equidistant (fisheye) projection.",
          "properties": {
            "type": {
              "const": "equidistant",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "type"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      ]
    },
    "RigLaserlineDataset": {
      "description": "Dataset for rig-level laserline calibration.\n\nEach view contains one row of the `(view, camera)` observation grid.\nUse [`RigLaserlineDataset::new`] to construct — it validates that every\nview has exactly `num_cameras` slots in both `cameras` and `laser_pixels`.\n\n# Missing-observation convention\n\n* `Some(obs)` — camera contributed data; `obs` may still be empty (no\n  correspondences / pixels), in which case it contributes zero residuals.\n* `None` — camera is absent for this view and is skipped entirely.\n\n# Example\n\n```no_run\n# use vision_calibration_optim::{RigLaserlineDataset, RigLaserlineView};\n// Two views, two cameras; camera 1 missed the target in view 0.\nlet views = vec![\n    RigLaserlineView {\n        cameras:      vec![Some(/* cam0 obs */ todo!()), None],\n        laser_pixels: vec![Some(vec![]),                None],\n    },\n    RigLaserlineView {\n        cameras:      vec![Some(/* cam0 obs */ todo!()), Some(/* cam1 obs */ todo!())],\n        laser_pixels: vec![Some(vec![]),                 Some(vec![])],\n    },\n];\nlet dataset = RigLaserlineDataset::new(views, 2).unwrap();\nassert_eq!(dataset.num_cameras, 2);\nassert_eq!(dataset.num_views(), 2);\n```",
      "properties": {
        "num_cameras": {
          "description": "Number of cameras in the rig; governs the expected slot count per view.",
          "format": "uint",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "views": {
          "description": "Per-view observation rows; length = number of views.\n\nEach `RigLaserlineView` contains two `Vec`s of length `num_cameras`,\none for target correspondences and one for laser pixels.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/RigLaserlineView"
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "views",
        "num_cameras"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RigLaserlineView": {
      "description": "Per-view observations for a rig-level laserline calibration.\n\nBoth `cameras` and `laser_pixels` are indexed by `cam_idx ∈ [0, num_cameras)`.\nA slot is `None` when that camera had no usable data in this view (occlusion,\nout-of-FOV, etc.).  An empty inner `Vec` is accepted but treated the same as\n`None` by the solver.",
      "properties": {
        "cameras": {
          "description": "Target correspondences per camera (`cam_idx` → `Option<CorrespondenceView>`).\n\n`None` means the camera did not see the calibration target in this view.\nThe slice length must equal `RigLaserlineDataset::num_cameras`.",
          "items": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/CorrespondenceView"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "laser_pixels": {
          "description": "Laser pixel observations per camera (`cam_idx` → `Option<Vec<Pt2>>`).\n\n`None` means the camera has no usable laser data for this view.\nThe slice length must equal `RigLaserlineDataset::num_cameras`.",
          "items": {
            "items": {
              "items": {
                "format": "double",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "maxItems": 2,
              "minItems": 2,
              "type": "array"
            },
            "type": [
              "array",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "cameras",
        "laser_pixels"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RigUpstreamCalibration": {
      "description": "Upstream rig calibration (frozen starting point).\n\nMirrors a rig hand-eye result's per-camera parameters + cam→rig poses,\nplus the per-view rig→target poses the downstream laserline dataset\nspans. Each camera is evaluated in its own model: any distortion kind,\nand an identity or Scheimpflug sensor.",
      "properties": {
        "cam_se3_rig": {
          "description": "Per-camera extrinsics `cam_se3_rig` (T_C_R).",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Iso3Schema"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "cameras": {
          "description": "Per-camera parameters, each in its camera's model.",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/CameraParams"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "rig_se3_target": {
          "description": "Per-view rig poses `rig_se3_target` (T_R_T).",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Iso3Schema"
          },
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "cameras",
        "cam_se3_rig",
        "rig_se3_target"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "SensorParams": {
      "description": "Serializable sensor model parameters.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "description": "Identity sensor model.",
          "properties": {
            "type": {
              "const": "identity",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "type"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "description": "Homography applied in the sensor plane.",
          "properties": {
            "h": {
              "description": "Row-major homography matrix mapping normalized to sensor coordinates.",
              "items": {
                "items": {
                  "format": "double",
                  "type": "number"
                },
                "maxItems": 3,
                "minItems": 3,
                "type": "array"
              },
              "maxItems": 3,
              "minItems": 3,
              "type": "array"
            },
            "type": {
              "const": "homography",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "type",
            "h"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "description": "Scheimpflug/tilted sensor model.",
          "properties": {
            "tilt_x": {
              "description": "Tilt around X axis in radians (alias: tau_x).",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "tilt_y": {
              "description": "Tilt around Y axis in radians (alias: tau_y).",
              "format": "double",
              "type": "number"
            },
            "type": {
              "const": "scheimpflug",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "type",
            "tilt_x",
            "tilt_y"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "description": "Input for rig laserline calibration: dataset + frozen upstream calibration.",
  "properties": {
    "dataset": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/RigLaserlineDataset",
      "description": "Per-view, per-camera observations."
    },
    "initial_planes_cam": {
      "description": "Optional per-camera initial plane in camera frame. If `None`, defaults\nto a generic `z=-0.2m` plane.",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/LaserPlane"
      },
      "type": [
        "array",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "upstream": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/RigUpstreamCalibration",
      "description": "Upstream rig calibration (frozen)."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "dataset",
    "upstream"
  ],
  "title": "RigLaserlineDeviceInput",
  "type": "object"
}
